From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 06:33:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a window tells the compositor which display it
 covers

#421 gave every display a window and every one of them draws the same
thing: they all load the same shell and lay their `<Screen>` regions out
in the desktop's coordinates, so the second monitor shows the desktop's
top-left corner rather than the region belonging to it.

A window has to say which display it is, and the BROWSER is what knows.
It put that window on that display -- `domicile_shell_windows.cc`
created it at that display's bounds -- so the answer is a lookup here,
on the UI thread, where the frame's view and the screen both are. Asking
the page instead would be asking it to work out which monitor it is from
its own geometry, and a guess is exactly how this area produces a
monitor showing another monitor's desktop.

So the binder reads it and hands it to the control channel, which states
it on the socket right after the handshake. The page never learns it and
no shell has to do anything: the compositor answers with the desktop
narrowed to that one display, moved to the origin, and a page goes on
laying out in the coordinates it always did.

`ScreenOf` is empty where there is nothing to name -- no display::Screen
at all, which is a unit test, and a frame with no view, which never made
it to a window. Then nothing is sent and the compositor describes the
whole desktop, which is what a nested run is.
---
 chrome/browser/chrome_browser_interface_binders.cc | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_interface_binders.cc b/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_interface_binders.cc
index 0de5171..a3d5250 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_interface_binders.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_interface_binders.cc
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 #include "chrome/browser/chrome_browser_interface_binders.h"
 
 #include "base/task/bind_post_task.h"
+#include "chrome/browser/domicile/domicile_shell_windows.h"
 #include "components/domicile/browser/control_channel.h"
 #include "components/domicile/browser/keyboard_layout.h"
 #include "components/domicile/browser/web_view_guest.h"
@@ -511,7 +512,15 @@ void PopulateChromeFrameBinders(
                 &domicile::BindControlChannel, std::move(receiver),
                 base::BindPostTask(
                     content::GetUIThreadTaskRunner({}),
-                    base::BindRepeating(&domicile::SetProcessKeymap))));
+                    base::BindRepeating(&domicile::SetProcessKeymap)),
+                // AND WHICH WINDOW THIS PAGE IS. A desk of several monitors is
+                // several windows, each loading the same shell, and the only
+                // thing that differs between them is the display they cover.
+                // Read here, on the UI thread, where the frame's view and the
+                // screen both are -- and read from the browser rather than
+                // asked of the page, which does not know which monitor it was
+                // put on and could only guess from its own geometry.
+                domicile::ScreenOf(frame)));
       }));
 
   // Domicile's engine fork: a <webview> asking for a guest to put behind it.
